---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/article.css';

const TITLE = 'Privacy Policy | ReflexLab';
const DESCRIPTION =
  'Privacy policy for ReflexLab. Learn how your data is handled. All data is stored locally in your browser and nothing is sent to external servers.';
---

<BaseLayout title={TITLE} description={DESCRIPTION} path="/privacy" topbarLabel="Privacy">
  <article class="article-container">
    <header class="article-header">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span class="breadcrumbs-separator">/</span>
        <span class="breadcrumbs-current">Privacy Policy</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="article-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="article-subtitle">Your privacy matters. Here's how ReflexLab handles your data.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="article-content">
      <p class="article-intro">
        ReflexLab is designed to be a privacy-friendly tool. We don't require accounts, we don't
        track you, and your test data never leaves your device.
      </p>

      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Data Storage</h2>
        <p>
          All data generated by using ReflexLab, including your reaction time results, personal
          best, session history, achieved ranks, and settings, is stored locally in your browser
          using localStorage.
        </p>
        <p>
          This means your data stays on your device. Nothing is sent to or stored on any external
          server. It also means your data won't sync across different browsers or devices.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>No Accounts or Sign-Ups</h2>
        <p>
          ReflexLab does not require you to create an account, provide an email address, or sign in.
          You can use the tool immediately without providing any personal information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          ReflexLab itself does not set any cookies. Your preferences and test data are stored using
          localStorage, which is separate from cookies and is not sent with network requests.
        </p>
        <p>
          However, Google Analytics sets cookies to distinguish unique visitors and track usage
          patterns. These cookies do not contain personally identifiable information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Third-Party Resources</h2>
        <p>ReflexLab loads the following external resources to provide its functionality:</p>
        <ul class="article-list">
          <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> (google.com) - anonymous usage analytics</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          While ReflexLab itself does not track you, this provider may log standard server access
          information (such as IP addresses) as part of its normal operations. Please refer to its
          privacy policy for more details.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          ReflexLab uses Google Analytics to collect anonymous usage data such as page views,
          approximate location (country/region), device type, and browser information. This helps us
          understand how the site is used and where we can improve.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google Analytics uses cookies to distinguish unique users. No personally identifiable
          information is collected. You can opt out of Google Analytics by using a browser extension
          or adjusting your browser's cookie settings.
        </p>
        <p>
          For more information, see{' '}
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Google's Privacy Policy</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Deleting Your Data</h2>
        <p>
          You can delete all your stored data at any time by using the Reset button in the toolbar
          above the test area. This will clear your personal best, session history, trend graph
          data, and achieved ranks.
        </p>
        <p>
          Alternatively, you can clear your browser's localStorage for this site through your
          browser settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="article-section">
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          If this privacy policy is updated, the changes will be reflected on this page. As
          ReflexLab grows and new features are added, this policy will be updated accordingly.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>

  <section class="disclaimer-section">
    <p class="disclaimer">
      <strong>Disclaimer:</strong> This reaction time test is for entertainment and personal tracking
      purposes. Results are affected by your device's hardware, browser performance, and network conditions.
      For scientific or medical assessments, please use calibrated laboratory equipment.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .disclaimer-section {
    padding: var(--space-xl) 0 0;
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--line-subtle);
  }

  .disclaimer {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    font-size: var(--text-label-size);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
